title: 'pallet-validator-collators: store MaxCollators as CollatorDraw'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The new enum `CollatorDraw` sets how many validators of the stored set are drawn as
    collators: `None` draws no validator, `UpTo(n)` up to `n` validators with registered keys, and
    `All` every validator with registered keys. Every variant draws in random order, and a
    validator that registers keys after a draw waits for the next validator set or cap change.

    `MaxCollators` stores a `CollatorDraw` with `DefaultMaxCollators` as default, and
    `set_max_collators` takes one.

    The new migration `MigrateV0ToV1` rewrites a cap stored as `u32` as `UpTo(cap)`. Without a
    stored cap, `MaxCollators` reads `DefaultMaxCollators`, and when a validator set is stored the
    migration draws the collators again under it, as `set_max_collators` does.

    Asset Hub Westend and People Westend run the migration.
crates:
- name: pallet-validator-collators
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-validator-set-announcer
  bump: none
